# Examples from the Classroom

Here are some examples of ways teachers are using AI to support their role as an educator.


<div style="max-width:900px; margin:40px auto; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">

<!-- Quote 1 -->
<div style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-start; margin:25px 0;">
<div style="max-width:70%; background-color:#b2dee3; border-radius:40px; padding:24px; box-shadow:0 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); position:relative;">
<div style="font-size:40px; opacity:0.35;">&ldquo;</div>
<div style="line-height:1.6; font-size:16px;">Writing rubrics used to take me forever. Now I can get a solid first draft in minutes and tweak it to fit my class.</div>
<div style="font-size:40px; text-align:right; opacity:0.35;">&rdquo;</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Quote 2 -->
<div style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; margin:25px 0;">
<div style="max-width:70%; background-color:#ffd199; border-radius:40px; padding:24px; box-shadow:0 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08); position:relative;">
<div style="font-size:40px; opacity:0.35;">&ldquo;</div>
<div style="line-height:1.6; font-size:16px;">One of my favorite uses is creating multiple versions of the same activity so I can better support students at different levels.</div>
<div style="font-size:40px; text-align:right; opacity:0.35;">&rdquo;</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Quote 3 -->
<div style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-start; margin:25px 0;">
<div style="max-width:70%; background-color:#b2dee3; border-radius:40px; padding:24px; box-shadow:0 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
<div style="font-size:40px; opacity:0.35;">&ldquo;</div>
<div style="line-height:1.6; font-size:16px;">I use [AI] to help draft parent emails and newsletters. It saves me a lot of time.</div>
<div style="font-size:40px; text-align:right; opacity:0.35;">&rdquo;</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- Quote 4 -->
<div style="display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; margin:25px 0;">
<div style="max-width:70%; background-color:#ffd199; border-radius:40px; padding:24px; box-shadow:0 6px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
<div style="font-size:40px; opacity:0.35;">&ldquo;</div>
<div style="line-height:1.6; font-size:16px;">AI gives me ideas I wouldn't have thought of on my own.</div>
<div style="font-size:40px; text-align:right; opacity:0.35;">&rdquo;</div>
</div>
</div>

</div>



> **💬 Quick Reflection:** Have you done anything similar in your teaching practice? Or have you seen teachers at your school use AI in similar ways?
MARKDOWN
